=\"region region-content-sidebar\">\n    <div class=\"views-element-container block block-views block-views-blocksyllabus-course-block-1\" id=\"block-yale-oyc-views-block-syllabus-course-block-1\">\n  \n    \n      <div><div class=\"view view-syllabus-course view-id-syllabus_course view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-5ad0d9e5449d00282dcea42ab73e46b616cb4332871f88cc327be5b41dc844dd\">\n  \n    \n      \n      <div class=\"view-content\">\n          <div class=\"views-row\">    <div class=\"views-field views-field-field-course-about-the-professor\"><div class=\"field-content\"><b>About Professor Jonathan Holloway</b>\n\n<p><p>Jonathan Holloway was Professor of History, African American Studies, and American Studies at Yale University and Dean of Yale College. He is the author of <em>Confronting the Veil: Abram Harris Jr., E. Franklin Frazier, and Ralph Bunche, 1919-1941</em> (2002) and <em>Jim Crow Wisdom: Memory and Identity in Black America Since 1940 </em>(2013); the editor of Ralph Bunche's <em>A Brief and Tentative Analysis of Negro Leadership</em> (2005); and the co-editor of the anthology <em>Black Scholars on the Line: Race, Social Science, and American Thought in the 20th Century</em> (2007). Professor Holloway received his PhD from Yale in 1995.</p><p>Learn more about Professor Holloway's book&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.uncpress.unc.edu/browse/book_detail?title_id=3419\"><em>Jim Crow Wisdom: Memory and Identity in Black America Since 1940</em></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></p> </p></div></div>  </div>\n\n    </div>\n  \n          </div>\n</div>\n\n  </div>\n\n  </div>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\n\t\t<div class=\"content-bottom\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t</main>\n\n\t<footer class=\"footer\" role=\"contentinfo\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"footer__inner\">\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"footer__logo-txt\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"topper-logo\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"http://www.yale.edu\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYale\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\